# 9. SHIPPING SERVICES — TWO INDEPENDENT WORKFLOWS

This is essential to the original product.

### WORKFLOW A — SHIPPING ONLY

Customer creates a shipment without booking warehouse storage.

Flow:

Customer → Create Shipment → Pickup Request → Driver Assignment → Pickup → Transit → Delivery → Proof of Delivery

Do not force storage booking.

### WORKFLOW B — WAREHOUSE + SHIPPING

Customer books warehouse storage.

Flow:

Customer → Storage Booking → Warehouse Approval → Receiving → Putaway → Inventory → Request Dispatch → Picking → Shipping → Delivery

Both workflows must use shared shipment and customer records where appropriate.

They must not be implemented as disconnected modules.

